        "instruction": "Decide the exact words to be submitted to the UI as the result of P.",
        "value": "# Gemini Supervisor Skill Specification & Operational Manual\n\n## 1. Canonical Rule Set and File Paths\n- **Canonical Agents.md**: `/Agents.md` (root directory). This is the sole authoritative definition of all bootstrap requirements, procedure steps (Steps 0–4), supervisory gates, and failure examples. No other copies or summaries may be substituted.\n- **Interface / Trigger File**: `/nextmessage.json`\n- **Isolated Run Artifact Directory**: `/ChatMachines/GeminiSupervisor/runs/<run_nonce>/`\n  - `state.json`: Execution run state and pointers (`current_state.run_nonce`).\n  - `messages.json`: Turn-by-turn conversation and semantic-operator exchanges.\n  - `store/store.json`: Persistent storage mirror of exchanges and step return schemas.\n\n## 2. Recommended Repository Layout Separation\nTo maintain a clean separation between source/engine logic and dynamic per-run streams:\n```text\n├── Agents.md                                 # Canonical rule set (immutable root reference)\n├── nextmessage.json                          # Active trigger interface\n├── src/                                      # Supervisor engine source, validators, and scripts\n├── config/                                   # Workflow and runtime configurations\n└── ChatMachines/GeminiSupervisor/runs/       # Per-run execution streams\n    └── <run_nonce>/                          # Isolated run container\n        ├── state.json\n        ├── messages.json\n        └── store/\n            └── store.json\n```\nMoving source code and utilities into `/src/` and `/config/` leaves the root clean for `Agents.md`, `nextmessage.json`, and run-stream tracking.\n\n## 3. Exact `nextmessage.json` Schema\nTo initiate or continue a run, `/nextmessage.json` must be written with the following exact JSON structure:\n```json\n{\n  \"run_nonce\": \"<path-safe unique run identifier>\",\n  \"nonce\": \"<unique request nonce>\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"<ISO 8601 UTC timestamp>\",\n  \"user_request\": \"<verbatim user message>\",\n  \"action\": \"step_execute | supervisory_evaluate\",\n  \"target_step\": \"Step_0 | Step_1 | Step_2 | Step_3 | Step_4\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"canonical_rules_path\": \"Agents.md\",\n    \"run_dir\": \"ChatMachines/GeminiSupervisor/runs/<run_nonce>/\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## 4. Mechanical Trigger & Execution Sequence\n1. **Bootstrap Turn**:\n   - Generate a unique path-safe alphanumeric string for `run_nonce` (e.g., `run_20260408_9f8c2b7d4e1a0f3c`).\n   - Initialize `/ChatMachines/GeminiSupervisor/runs/<run_nonce>/` with `state.json`, `messages.json`, and `store/store.json` containing matching `run_nonce` values.\n   - Write `/nextmessage.json` with the user request and target step.\n   - Commit `/nextmessage.json` to the repo to actuate the run.\n2. **Step Execution Turn**:\n   - The executor reads `/nextmessage.json` and canonical `/Agents.md`.\n   - The executor performs the specified step and appends the complete return schema to `/ChatMachines/GeminiSupervisor/runs/<run_nonce>/messages.json` and `/store/store.json`.\n   - Do not perform the Supervisory Gate during step execution.\n3. **Supervisory Gate Turn**:\n   - The supervisor reads the execution return schema from `/messages.json`.\n   - The supervisor computes the granular mirror and step-level evaluation, verifying whether any failure pattern matches.\n   - If `gate_result` is `PASS`, the transition controller advances to the next step. If `FAIL`, the step must be repeated."
      }
